{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-62643","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120288","text":"R0.9 — nc35's kernel leg: cases A and B on real kernel WireGuard (plan)"}]},{"id":"blk-62644","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120289","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: DRAFT, prespecified 2026-09-30 by the Claude session on the Mac, at Travis's go. Not reviewed by GPT. Nothing is built or run."},{"id":"spn-120290","text":" On review: freeze it, then build in the order in §5. This is GPT's execution-order item 9 (R0.9-OPEN §8a). "},{"id":"spn-120291","marks":["code"],"text":"lab/scripts/nc35_layer_substitution.sh"},{"id":"spn-120292","text":" says it itself: "},{"id":"spn-120293","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"The scripted transport is NOT the claim -- it is the harness … The kernel-WireGuard execution of A and B is a separate leg.\""},{"id":"spn-120294","text":" This file is that leg's contract, written before its code."}]},{"id":"blk-62645","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120295","text":"1. What the leg must show, and nothing more"}]},{"id":"blk-62646","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120296","text":"The cases keep nc35's letters and nc35's expected values ("},{"id":"spn-120297","marks":["code"],"text":"nc35_layer_substitution.sh"},{"id":"spn-120298","text":" lines 145–156)."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-62648","spans":[{"id":"spn-120299","text":"Case"}]},{"id":"blk-62649","spans":[{"id":"spn-120300","text":"Setup"}]},{"id":"blk-62650","spans":[{"id":"spn-120301","text":"Kernel evidence required"}]},{"id":"blk-62651","spans":[{"id":"spn-120302","text":"Connector result required"}]}],"id":"blk-62647","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-62652","spans":[{"id":"spn-120303","marks":["bold"],"text":"A"}]},{"id":"blk-62653","spans":[{"id":"spn-120304","text":"Right "},{"id":"spn-120305","marks":["code"],"text":"PeerExpectation"},{"id":"spn-120306","text":" (N1, K1). The endpoint is held by a DIFFERENT WireGuard peer (K2)."}]},{"id":"blk-62654","